+    /// other) and then runs miniscript's `update_input_with_descriptor` /
+    /// `update_output_with_descriptor`, which writes them again from the descriptor, with their
+    /// leaf hashes, and also sets the scripts and the taproot internal key and merkle root. Keys
+    /// the descriptor does not contain, signatures and every other field are left as they are.
